<title>USA: U.S. brass mill receipts dip in February - ABMS.</title>
<headline>U.S. brass mill receipts dip in February - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brass mill receipts in February fell to 88,021 short tons of contained copper, down from 104,818 short tons in January, the American Bureau of Metal Statistics said.</p>
<p>Brass mill shipments in February, including copper semis, copper alloy semis and scrap totaled 144,875 short tons of contained copper, down slightly from a revised 146,922 tons in January.</p>
<p>Brass mill inventory of refinery shapes, materials in process and scrap at the end of February totaled 144,729 short tons of contained copper, barely changed from January's 144,939 tons.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
